# Code owners — review that a CI gate cannot substitute for.
#
# Flyway migrations are listed because artifact rollback (ADR-028/029) depends
# on every migration being expand-only, and `scripts/check-migration-safety.sh`
# can only catch the unambiguous breaks. The judgement calls it cannot make —
# a constraint tightened rather than widened, a backfill that assumes the new
# code is already deployed, a change that is technically additive but
# semantically incompatible — are exactly what a human review is for.
/backend/persistence/src/main/resources/db/migration/ @yannisyoussef

# The deployment contract with the Infinity Ops platform: what GitHub sends,
# what it is allowed to hold, and what a green run is permitted to claim
# (ADR-030). A change here can quietly reintroduce a host credential or turn a
# handoff back into a false deployment success.
/.github/workflows/                                   @yannisyoussef
/scripts/gitlab-handoff.sh                            @yannisyoussef
/scripts/check-migration-safety.sh                    @yannisyoussef
/scripts/validate-image-digest.sh                     @yannisyoussef
/deploy/                                              @yannisyoussef

